{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery. Only in deadlock (all sides blocked) is full_rotate allowed. The design avoids oscillations and ensures rapid return to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
  "G": [
